<article class="env-lemma" id="06FJ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/06FJ">Lemma <span data-tag="06FJ">100.9.12</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. The rule $\mathcal{U} \mapsto |\mathcal{U}|$ defines an inclusion preserving bijection between open substacks of $\mathcal{X}$ and open subsets of $|\mathcal{X}|$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Choose a presentation $[U/R] \to \mathcal{X}$, see Algebraic Stacks, Lemma <a href="/tag/04T5" data-tag="04T5">94.16.2</a>. By Lemma <a href="/tag/0507" data-tag="0507">100.9.11</a> we see that open substacks correspond to $R$-invariant open subschemes of $U$. On the other hand Lemmas <a href="/tag/04XJ" data-tag="04XJ">100.4.5</a> and <a href="/tag/04XL" data-tag="04XL">100.4.7</a> guarantee these correspond bijectively to open subsets of $|\mathcal{X}|$. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>